<title>FRANCE: French regulator backs French insurance merger.</title>
<headline>French regulator backs French insurance merger.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Financial Markets Committee, the CMF, said on Tuesday it had approved a planned merger between insurers AXA and UAP.</p>
<p>The regulator said in a statement it had met on November 18 to review the planned share swap and judged it to be valid.  </p>
<p>The public offer will open after publication of an official note by the COB stock exchange watchdog and various insurance and credit company approvals, the CMF said.</p>
<p>AXA and UAP said on November 12 they planned a merger to create the world's second biggest insurer.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
